\n\n**0527 SR-4 (API list, lines 24-79):** Only defines 4 APIs: `POST /api/session/register`, `POST /api/session/close`, `GET /api/sessions`, `GET /api/session/:id`. No mention of `/api/issue/*` anywhere in the 0527 files.\n\n---\n\n### Inconsistency 5: `GET /api/sessions` and `GET /api/session/:id` -- new APIs not in 0526\n\n**0526 file (section 6, API table):** Only lists 3 API groups: `/api/session/register`, `/api/session/close`, `/api/issue/*`. No read/query APIs.\n\n**0527 SR-4 (lines 67-79):** Adds two new GET endpoints: `GET /api/sessions` (with query parameter filtering by machine_id, project_slug, status) and `GET /api/session/:id` (single session details). These query APIs are completely absent from the 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### Inconsistency 6: Backend data storage format -- JSON map vs. SQLite tables\n\n**0526 file (section 4, lines 144-157):** Shows the backend data structure as a flat JSON map keyed by session_id:\n```json\n{\n  \"bf15cac4-...\": {\n    \"machine_id\": \"...\",\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\nThis is a simple key-value structure with no separate machines or projects tables.\n\n**0526 file (section 10, lines 420-492):** Also defines full SQLite schema with 3 normalized tables (sessions, machines, projects) with indexes.\n\n**0527 SR-4:** Only defines the SQLite schema (3 tables), no mention of a JSON map format. The 0526 file has both representations (JSON in section 4, SQL in section 10), which is potentially confusing but not strictly contradictory since section 4 may be illustrative. The 0527 files resolve this by only using the SQL schema.\n\n---\n\n### Inconsistency 7: `check_proxy_active()` function placement\n\n**0526 file (section 5.1, line 213):** States the function goes into `hooks/base.sh`:\n> \"**检测逻辑**（共享函数，放入 `hooks/base.sh`）\"\n\n**0527 SR-2 (line 32, section \"代理状态检测\"):** Says:\n> \"由 `hooks/base.sh` 中的 `check_proxy_active()` 共享函数完成（详见设计文档 5.1 节）\"\n\n**0527 SR-5 (line 32):** Same reference to `hooks/base.sh`.\n\n**Verdict:** Consistent across all files -- all point to `hooks/base.sh`. No actual inconsistency here.\n\n---\n\n### Inconsistency 8: Machines table `os` field -- source ambiguity\n\n**0526 file (section 10.2, machines table, line 468):** Shows `os TEXT NOT NULL` with comment \"platform.sh\" as source.\n\n**0527 SR-2 (register_session hook code):** Only the `sessions` table receives the `os` field in the POST request. The `machines` table data (hostname, username, os) is not explicitly part of the hook's POST body -- it's derived server-side.\n\n**0527 SR-4 (POST /register processing, lines 42-43):** Says \"INSERT OR IGNORE to machines table, UPDATE last_seen_at\" but does not specify where `os`, `hostname`, `username` come from for the machines table. The POST request body does not contain `hostname` or `username` as separate fields -- only `machine_id` (which is `whoami@hostname` combined) and `os`.\n\n**Verdict:** The 0527 files have a gap: the machines table requires `hostname` and `username` as separate columns, but the POST /register request only sends the combined `machine_id` string. The backend would need to parse `machine_id` back into `hostname` and `username`, which is not specified in any 0527 file. The 0526 file section 10.1 field source table (line 457) also does not address this since it only covers the sessions table fields.\n\n---\n\n### Inconsistency 9: Verification criteria -- machines/projects auto-creation detail level\n\n**0526 file (section 11.2, line 592):** Verification item states:\n> \"machines 表和 projects 表自动 INSERT OR IGNORE，`last_seen_at` 更新\"\n\n**0527 SR-2 (verification, line 89):** Only states:\n> \"注册请求包含所有 8 个字段\"\n\nThe SR-2 verification does not mention machines/projects table verification at all (it is a hook-level spec, not a backend spec). The machines/projects verification is instead in SR-4 (line 177):\n> \"POST `/api/session/register` 正确写入三张表\"\n\nThis is a scope allocation difference rather than a contradiction -- the 0526 file has al