no reference to it at all.\n\n**Files involved**: `00-overview.md`, `database-schema.md` (0527) vs Section 3.3 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Status API `previous_status` response field -- new addition\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.4, B4):\n- The `/api/issue/status` response is not explicitly defined with a full response schema. Only a request example is shown. No `previous_status` field is mentioned.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`):\n- Defines a full response schema including `previous_status` (the old status before update) and `updated_at` fields.\n- `previous_status` is used to drive `_sync_github_label()` for label removal.\n- Returns error responses for `not_owner` and `invalid_transition` which are not in the 0526 file.\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-status-api.md` (0527) vs Section 5.4 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Status API adds `reviewing` intermediate state and changes skill trigger points\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.4, table):\n- `003-9-issue-review` has two entries: merge triggers `merged`, reject triggers `rejected`.\n- No `reviewing` status is triggered by 003-9-issue-review.\n- GitHub operations for 003-5-issue-fix: only \"gh issue comment\" (no label change).\n- GitHub operations for 003-6-issue-done: `gh issue edit --remove-label \"in-progress\" --add-label \"ready-for-pr\"`.\n- GitHub operations for 003-9-issue-review merge: `gh issue close`.\n- GitHub operations for 003-9-issue-review reject: `gh issue edit --add-label \"rejected\"`.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md`):\n- Adds a new `reviewing` status triggered at the **start** of 003-9-issue-review (before merge/reject decision).\n- GitHub Label changes are now fully automated via `_sync_github_label()` inside `update_issue_status()`:\n  - 003-5-issue-fix: changes labels from `in-progress` to `fixing` (0526 had no label change for fixing).\n  - 003-6-issue-done: changes from `fixing` to `ready-for-pr` (0526 changed from `in-progress` to `ready-for-pr`).\n  - 003-9-issue-review: adds `reviewing` label first (entirely new step).\n- Skill scripts no longer need to manually call `gh issue edit --add-label/--remove-label` -- all label management is centralized in `backend.sh`.\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-status-api.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md` (0527) vs Section 5.4 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 5. GitHub Label for `fixing` status -- contradictory\n\n**0526 file** (Section 4.1, status table):\n- `fixing` status: GitHub operation is \"—（由 issue-fix 技能触发）\" -- meaning **no** GitHub label operation for the `fixing` state.\n\n**0527 file** (`database-schema.md`, status enum table; `backend-infrastructure.md`, label mapping):\n- `fixing` maps to GitHub label `fixing` (explicitly listed as a label to be synced).\n- `_status_to_label()` in `backend-infrastructure.md` maps `fixing` to label `\"fixing\"`.\n- `fix-to-review-skills.md` shows label transition `in-progress` to `fixing` when 003-5-issue-fix runs.\n\n**Files involved**: `database-schema.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md` (0527) vs Section 4.1 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 6. GitHub Label for `pr-created`, `testing`, `reviewing` statuses -- contradictory\n\n**0526 file** (Section 4.1):\n- `pr-created`: GitHub operation is \"—\" (no label).\n- `testing`: GitHub operation is \"—\" (no label).\n- `reviewing`: GitHub operation is \"—\" (no label).\n\n**0527 file** (`database-schema.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md`):\n- `pr-created` maps to label `pr-created`.\n- `testing` maps to label `testing`.\n- `reviewing` maps to label `reviewing`.\n- All three have explicit label management in `_status_to_label()`.\n\n**Files involved**: `database-schema.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md` (0527) vs Section 4.1 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 7. New labels required in `labels.conf` -- expanded scope\n\n**0526 file** (Section 4.1):\n- Implies labels `in-progress`, `ready-for-pr`, `rejected` based on the GitHub operations column.\n- `fixing`, `pr-created`, `testing`, `reviewing` are NOT listed as labels to be created on GitHub.\n\n**0527 file** (`database-schema.md`):\n- Explicitly states: \"GitHub Label 需要在 `003-1-issue-init` 的 `labels.conf` 中定义：`in-progress`、`fixing`、`ready-for-pr`、`pr-created`、`testing`、`reviewing`、`rejected`。\"\n- This adds 4 new labels (`fixing`, `pr-created`, `testing`, `reviewing`) that the 0526 design did not require.\n\n**Files involved**: `database-schema.md` (0527) vs Section 4.1 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 8. New entity: `backend.sh` shared module -- entirely new\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No shared module concept. Each skill script directly uses `curl` inline, reading `backend.conf` and constructing API calls manually in each script.\n\n**0527 file** (`backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/claim-skill.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md`):\n- Introduces `.claude/skills/backend.sh` as a shared module with functions: `_load_backend_url()`, `_backend_available()`, `_call_backend()`, `_get_session_id()`, `_status_to_label()`, `_sync_github_label()`, `update_issue_status()`.\n- All skill scripts are instructed to `source \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/skills/backend.sh\"` at the top.\n- Centralizes URL reading, health checks, HTTP calls, and GitHub label sync.\n\n**Files involved**: `backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/claim-skill.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md` (0527) -- no equivalent in 0526.\n\n---\n\n### 9. New entity: `/health` health check endpoint -- entirely new\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No health check endpoint mentioned.\n\n**0527 file** (`backend-infrastructure.md`):\n- Defines `GET /health` endpoint returning `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"uptime\": 3600}`.\n- Used by `_backend_available()` for pre-flight backend availability checks.\n\n**Files involved**: `backend-infrastructure.md` (0527) -- no equivalent in 0526.\n\n---\n\n### 10. New entity: `claude-tap-plus backend` CLI subcommand -- entirely new\n\n**0526 file**:\n- Mentions the backend as \"claude-tap-plus 后端服务器\" but does not specify how to start it. No CLI subcommand, no port, no database path arguments.\n\n**0527 file** (`backend-infrastructure.md`):\n- Defines `claude-tap-plus backend` as a CLI subcommand with `--port` (default 8080), `--db` (default `./backend.db`), and `--config` arguments.\n\n**Files involved**: `backend-infrastructure.md` (0527) vs Section 5.1 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 11. New entity: Degradation strategy (B8) -- entirely new\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No explicit degradation strategy. The 0526 file describes what the APIs do but does not define behavior when the backend is unavailable.\n\n**0527 file** (`degradation-strategy.md`):\n- Adds a complete degradation strategy document (B8) with specific behaviors for each API when backend is unavailable.\n- Key rule: `claim` API failure **blocks** the operation (the only blocking degradation); all other API failures are silent.\n- Introduces `--force` flag concept for claim to bypass backend in single-agent scenarios.\n\n**Files involved**: `degradation-strategy.md` (0527) -- no equivalent in 0526.\n\n---\n\n### 12. New entity: `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` environment variable discussion\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No mention of `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` as an environment variable. Session ID is always obtained via `json_get '.session_id'`.\n\n**0527 file** (`00-overview.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md`):\n- Explicitly discusses `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` as a potential environment variable.\n- `_get_session_id()` in `backend.sh` prioritizes `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env var, falling back to `json_get '.session_id'`.\n- States \"不要求模块 C 注入此环境变量\" but the code already supports it.\n\n**Files involved**: `00-overview.md`, `backend-infrastructure.md` (0527) vs 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 13. Status API error responses -- expanded\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No explicit error response definitions for the status API.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`):\n- Defines `not_owner` error (non-owner session trying to update).\n- Defines `invalid_transition` error (illegal state transition, optional).\n- Defines permission check logic: \"session_id 必须是当前领取者\".\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-status-api.md` (0527) vs Section 5.4 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 14. Claim API: `issue_title` field marked as optional\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.3):\n- The claim API request shows `issue_title` as a field in the example but does not specify whether it is required or optional.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-claim-api.md`):\n- Explicitly marks `issue_title` as **not required** (否 in the required column).\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-claim-api.md` (0527) vs Section 5.3 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 15. Claim API: New behavior for merged/rejected status\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.3):\n- The claim logic only checks if the status is `idle` for claiming. No explicit handling of `merged`/`rejected` states in claim logic description.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-claim-api.md`):\n- Explicitly states: \"如果状态是 merged/rejected → 返回 already_claimed\" (step 3d in business logic).\n- Adds verification criterion: \"已合并/打回的 issue 不可领取\".\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-claim-api.md` (0527) vs Section 5.3 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 16. Claim API: Re-claim after rejection + release\n\n**0526 file**:\n- No mention of re-claiming after a rejected issue is released.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-claim-api.md`):\n- Adds verification criterion: \"已打回的 issue 释放（status 恢复 idle）后可被重新领取\".\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-claim-api.md` (0527) -- no equivalent in 0526.\n\n---\n\n### 17. Legal state transitions: expanded and partially changed\n\n**0526 file** (Section 4.2):\n- The state flow diagram shows: `fixing` can go to `ready-for-pr` or loop back to `claimed` (reject).\n- `reviewing` can go to `merged` or loop back to `claimed` (reject).\n- No explicit `reviewing` to `fixing` transition shown.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`):\n- Defines explicit legal transitions list:\n  -