ition shown.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`):\n- Defines explicit legal transitions list:\n  - `claimed` to `fixing`\n  - `fixing` to `ready-for-pr`\n  - `fixing` to `claimed` (reject rollback)\n  - `ready-for-pr` to `pr-created`\n  - `pr-created` to `testing`\n  - `testing` to `reviewing`\n  - `reviewing` to `merged`\n  - `reviewing` to `fixing` (reject rollback) -- **different from 0526 which had `reviewing` to `claimed`**\n- Also notes \"是否严格校验流转路径可选\" (enforcement is optional).\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-status-api.md` (0527) vs Section 4.2 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 18. SessionEnd hook: `--max-time 5` timeout added\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.6):\n- The `release_session_issues()` curl call uses `curl -s -X POST` with no explicit timeout flag.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-release-api.md`, `skill-refactor/session-end-hook.md`):\n- The curl call adds `--max-time 5` timeout.\n- The session-end-hook doc explicitly notes: \"超时 5 秒，避免 session 结束时卡住\".\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-release-api.md`, `skill-refactor/session-end-hook.md` (0527) vs Section 5.6 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 19. Skill refactor: `claim-skill.md` uses `_sync_github_label` but claim script does not `source backend.sh`\n\n**0527 file** (`skill-refactor/claim-skill.md`):\n- The claim skill script defines its own `get_backend_url()` function instead of sourcing `backend.sh`.\n- But it calls `_sync_github_label \"$ISSUE_NUM\" \"\" \"claimed\"` which is a function defined in `backend.sh`.\n- The document does not show `source \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/skills/backend.sh\"` in the claim script, unlike the fix-to-review skills which do source it.\n\n**This is an internal inconsistency within the 0527 documents themselves**: the claim skill calls a function from `backend.sh` without sourcing it.\n\n**Files involved**: `skill-refactor/claim-skill.md` (0527).\n\n---\n\n### 20. `update_issue_status()` function signature and behavior -- new concept\n\n**0526 file**:\n- Each skill script manually constructs the curl call to `/api/issue/status` with inline JSON.\n- GitHub label operations are done separately in each skill script.\n\n**0527 file** (`backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md`):\n- Introduces `update_issue_status()` as a one-line function call: `update_issue_status \"$ISSUE_NUM\" \"fixing\"`.\n- This function internally handles: calling the backend API, extracting `previous_status`, and calling `_sync_github_label()` to remove old label and add new label.\n- Skill scripts no longer construct curl calls manually for status updates.\n- Skill scripts no longer call `gh issue edit --add-label/--remove-label` directly.\n\n**Files involved**: `backend-infrastructure.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md` (0527) vs Sections 5.4-5.5 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### 21. `003-9-issue-review` now has a `reviewing` step before merge/reject decision\n\n**0526 file** (Section 5.4):\n- 003-9-issue-review only has two outcomes: `merged` or `rejected`. No intermediate `reviewing` state.\n\n**0527 file** (`issue-status-api.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md`):\n- 003-9-issue-review first marks `reviewing` when the review begins, then marks `merged` or `rejected` after the decision.\n- This adds a new intermediate state and label sync that did not exist in the 0526 design.\n\n**Files involved**: `issue-status-api.md`, `skill-refactor/fix-to-review-skills.md` (0527) vs Section 5.4 of 0526 file.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Categories\n\n**Contradictions (direct conflicts):**\n- Items 4, 5, 6: The 0526 file says `fixing`, `pr-created`, `testing`, `reviewing` states have NO GitHub labels. The 0527 files say they all DO have corresponding labels.\n- Item 17: The reject path from `reviewing` goes to `claimed` in 0526 but to `fixing` in 0527.\n\n**New information added in 0527 (not present in 0526):**\n- Items 8, 9, 10, 11, 12: `backend.sh` shared module, `/health` endpoint, CLI subcommand, degradation strategy, `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` env var.\n- Items 13, 15, 16: Expanded error handling for status/claim APIs.\n\n**Differences in detail level (same intent, different specification):**\n- Items 1, 3, 14, 18: The 0527 files provide more precise specifications (field optionality, response schemas, timeouts).</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>0</total_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>97714</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
