[2026-05-27 22:08:07] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"7e8378a3-13bc-4994-91d5-44203e279146","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\7e8378a3-13bc-4994-91d5-44203e279146.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"default","agent_id":"ae27cc58253a8c6f1","agent_type":"general-purpose","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\7e8378a3-13bc-4994-91d5-44203e279146\\subagents\\agent-ae27cc58253a8c6f1.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"Now I have read all the files. Let me do a thorough comparison.\n\n---\n\nHere is the complete list of inconsistencies found between the 2026-05-27 module-D-requirements files and the 2026-05-26 design files (skill-integration-design.md, backend-design.md, and issue-design.md):\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 1: `reviewing` status is defined but never written\n\n**0526 files say** (skill-integration-design.md section IV, issue-design.md section 4.1): The `reviewing` status is listed as a valid status in the status table.\n\n**0527 files say** (00-overview.md \"status write timing\" table): No skill ever writes `reviewing`. The D6 (003-9-issue-review) module jumps directly from `testing` to `merged` or `rejected`. The `reviewing` status appears in the status definition table in 00-overview.md but has no corresponding writer in the timing table.\n\n**Files**: `00-overview.md` lines 119-132 (status table) vs. lines 162-174 (timing table); `D5-issue-test.md` writes `testing`; `D6-issue-review.md` writes `merged`/`rejected` with no intermediate `reviewing`.\n\n**Assessment**: The 0526 issue-design.md also has `reviewing` in the status flow diagram (arrows from `testing` to `reviewing` to `merged`), but the 0526 skill-integration-design.md timing table similarly never assigns any skill to write `reviewing`. Both versions have this gap -- the 0527 files carry it forward unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 2: D7 explicitly does NOT source backend.sh -- contradicts D0 architecture\n\n**0527 D0 says** (D0-backend-infra.md): All D1-D7 should `source \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/skills/backend.sh\"`.\n\n**0527 D7 says** (D7-session-end-release.md line 22): \"Note: Does NOT depend on backend.sh, directly inlines curl calls (hook environment is isolated from skill environment).\"\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.9): The D7 `release_session_issues()` is also shown as an inline curl call without sourcing backend.sh, which matches D7.\n\n**File**: `D7-session-end-release.md` vs. `D0-backend-infra.md`\n\n**Assessment**: D0 says all modules depend on `backend.sh`, but D7 explicitly opts out because the hook environment is separate from the skill environment. This is an internal inconsistency within the 0527 files, but it aligns with the 0526 file's approach.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 3: Backend URL discovery mechanism differs between 0526 session-design and 0527 D0\n\n**0526 session-design.md says** (section 5.1): The backend URL should be obtained from `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.proxy.json` via `check_proxy_active()`, which sets `PROXY_BACKEND_URL`. The hook detects whether the proxy is running by checking PID. No `.claude/backend.conf` file is needed for session management.\n\n**0527 D0 says** (D0-backend-infra.md): The backend URL is read from `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/backend.conf`, a per-project configuration file. There is no mention of `.proxy.json` or `check_proxy_active()`.\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.2, 9.3): Uses `.claude/backend.conf` -- consistent with 0527.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-session-design.md` (0526) vs. `D0-backend-infra.md` (0527) vs. `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` (0526)\n\n**Assessment**: Within the 0526 files themselves, there is already a conflict -- session-design.md uses `.proxy.json` for backend URL discovery while skill-integration-design.md uses `.claude/backend.conf`. The 0527 files chose the `backend.conf` approach exclusively, dropping the `.proxy.json` mechanism entirely for issue skill integration.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 4: SessionEnd hook responsibilities differ\n\n**0526 session-design.md says**: The `29-session-end/base.sh` hook is responsible for calling `POST /api/session/close` (session unregistration).\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.9): The `29-session-end/base.sh` hook calls `POST /api/issue/release-session` (issue release).\n\n**0527 D7 says** (D7-session-end-release.md): The `29-session-end/base.sh` hook is modified to add issue release. No mention of session close/unregister.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-session-design.md` vs. `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` vs. `D7-session-end-release.md`\n\n**Assessment**: Both session close and issue release need to happen in the same hook (`29-session-end/base.sh`). The 0527 D7 file only describes the issue release addition, but does not mention coexistence with the session close logic from the session design. If both designs are implemented, the same hook file would need both functions.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 5: `update_issue_status` function location\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.4): `update_issue_status()` is defined locally in each skill script (shown inline in the D2 code block).\n\n**0527 D0 says** (D0-backend-infra.md): `update_issue_status()` is defined as a shared function inside `.claude/skills/backend.sh`, sourced by all skills.\n\n**0527 D2-D6 say**: They all use `source \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/skills/backend.sh\"` and call `update_issue_status` without redefining it.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` section 5.4 vs. `D0-backend-infra.md` vs. `D2-issue-fix.md` through `D6-issue-review.md`\n\n**Assessment**: The 0527 files refactor `update_issue_status` from a per-script inline function into a shared module. This is a design improvement, not a contradiction, but it is a meaningful structural difference.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 6: CLAUDE_SESSION_ID injection -- different recommendations\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 9.1): \"Need to additionally inject CLAUDE_SESSION_ID\" -- the text presents it as a requirement, with the \"simpler way\" as an afterthought note.\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says**: Uses `json_get '.session_id'` without mentioning environment variable injection.\n\n**0527 D0 says** (D0-backend-infra.md, \"CLAUDE_SESSION_ID source explanation\" section): Explicitly recommends method 2 (`json_get '.session_id'`) as the current approach, and method 1 (environment variable) as a future possibility if module C implements it. The tone is reversed -- environment variable injection is secondary, not primary.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` section 9.1 vs. `D0-backend-infra.md` bottom section\n\n**Assessment**: The 0527 file changes the emphasis/priority. In 0526, env var injection is presented first and `json_get` as the simpler alternative. In 0527, `json_get` is the recommended current approach and env var is future work.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 7: `D2: issue-fix` description differs from backend-design.md\n\n**0526 backend-design.md says** (module D, row D2): \"D2: issue-fix -> worktree -- Upgrade to create worktree, inject issue info into CLAUDE.md\"\n\n**0527 D2 says** (D2-issue-fix.md): D2 is \"create branch then mark fixing status in backend.\" No mention of worktree creation or CLAUDE.md injection.\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.4): D2 is about marking `fixing` status -- no worktree mention.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-backend-design.md` (0526) vs. `D2-issue-fix.md` (0527) vs. `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` (0526)\n\n**Assessment**: The 0526 backend-design.md includes a \"Function 2 supplementary plan\" that describes upgrading D2 to worktree mode, but the 0526 skill-integration-design.md does not include this. The 0527 D2 file follows the skill-integration-design (no worktree), contradicting the backend-design's supplementary plan.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 8: `claimed_at` handling during release -- field treatment differs\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says** (section 10.4): During release, the SQL is `UPDATE ... SET status='idle', session_id=NULL, claimed_at=NULL` -- explicitly nullifies `claimed_at`.\n\n**0527 D7 says** (D7-session-end-release.md): \"Update remaining records' status to idle, session_id cleared.\" No mention of clearing `claimed_at`.\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (timing table): \"SessionEnd: UPDATE status='idle' (exclude merged/rejected)\" -- only mentions status update, not session_id or claimed_at.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-issue-design.md` section 10.4 vs. `D7-session-end-release.md` vs. `00-overview.md`\n\n**Assessment**: The 0526 issue-design is more thorough in specifying that both `session_id` AND `claimed_at` should be NULLed. The 0527 files are less precise about which fields get cleared during release.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 9: Architecture diagram text differs\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 5.1 architecture box): The label reads \"each skill script's backend call functions (_call_backend)\".\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (architecture box): The label reads \"backend call functions (backend.sh)\".\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` vs. `00-overview.md`\n\n**Assessment**: Reflects the refactoring from per-script functions to shared `backend.sh`, consistent with Inconsistency 5 above.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 10: SessionEnd release behavior for `rejected` status\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says** (section 10.3, query 4): `AND status NOT IN ('merged', 'rejected')` -- both `merged` AND `rejected` are excluded from release. The `rejected` status arrow in the state flow diagram (section 4.2) goes back to `reviewing`, not to `idle`.\n\n**0527 D7 says** (D7-session-end-release.md verification criteria line 78): \"`rejected` status issues are released to `idle` (can be reclaimed).\" This explicitly states rejected issues ARE released.\n\n**0527 D6 says** (D6-issue-review.md verification criteria line 82): \"rejected status issues can be reclaimed after SessionEnd release.\" Confirms rejected issues get released.\n\n**0527 degradation-testing.md says** (T07, T10): T10 says \"merged issues are not released after SessionEnd\" but makes no parallel statement about rejected. T07 says \"rejected issue is released after being freed and can be re-claimed.\"\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-issue-design.md` section 10.3 vs. `D7-session-end-release.md` vs. `D6-issue-review.md` vs. `degradation-testing.md`\n\n**Assessment**: This is a meaningful behavioral change. The 0526 design protects both `merged` and `rejected` from release. The 0527 design releases `rejected` issues so they can be re-claimed, while only protecting `merged`. This changes the state lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 11: `/api/issue/release-session` API visibility differs\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md architecture diagram** (section 5.1): Shows only 4 APIs in the backend box: `/api/issue/check`, `/api/issue/claim`, `/api/issue/status`, `/api/issue/release`. The `/api/issue/release-session` is NOT shown in the architecture diagram.\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md section 5.9**: Uses `/api/issue/release-session` in code.\n\n**0526 issue-design.md architecture diagram** (section 5.1): Shows all 5 APIs including `/api/issue/release-session`.\n\n**0527 00-overview.md architecture diagram**: Shows only 4 APIs: `/api/issue/check`, `/api/issue/claim`, `/api/issue/status`, `/api/issue/release`. Missing `/api/issue/release-session`.\n\n**0527 D0 says** (D0-backend-infra.md \"Backend APIs\" table): Lists all 6 APIs including both `/api/issue/release` and `/api/issue/release-session`.\n\n**Files**: `00-overview.md` vs. `D0-backend-infra.md` vs. `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` vs. `claude-tap-plus-issue-design.md`\n\n**Assessment**: The 0527 overview architecture diagram is missing `/api/issue/release-session` while D0's API table includes it. The 0526 skill-integration-design has the same gap in its architecture diagram.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 12: Data table for D7 in overview -- missing `release-session` API column\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (改造清单汇总 table, line 185): D7's backend API is listed as `/api/issue/release-session`.\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (各技能需要传入后端的数据汇总 table, line 85): D7 row says \"session_id only, release-session API handles internally.\"\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (改造清单汇总 table, line 437): D7's backend API is listed as `/api/issue/release-session`. Consistent.\n\n**Assessment**: These are consistent -- no inconsistency here, included for completeness of the comparison.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 13: Database schema -- index definitions differ\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says** (section 10.1): Defines three indexes:\n```sql\nCREATE INDEX idx_issue_claims_repo ON issue_claims(repo_full_name);\nCREATE INDEX idx_issue_claims_session ON issue_claims(session_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_issue_claims_status ON issue_claims(status);\n```\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (database table section): Shows the CREATE TABLE but does NOT include any CREATE INDEX statements.\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-issue-design.md` section 10.1 vs. `00-overview.md`\n\n**Assessment**: The 0527 overview omits the index definitions that the 0526 issue-design specifies. If the overview is used as the implementation reference, indexes would be missed.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 14: `issue_title` field -- when it is populated\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says** (section 10.1): `issue_title` is described as \"issue title (cached, for display convenience)\" -- populated only during claim.\n\n**0527 D1 says** (D1-issue-claim.md): The claim API request includes `issue_title`. Consistent.\n\n**0527 00-overview.md data table** (line 79): D1 (claim) includes `issue_title` in its data; D2-D6 do not. Consistent.\n\n**0526 backend-design.md says** (original requirements, point 6): \"issue-claim script needs to write backend service access script, passing issue unique ID, project GitHub address, project name into backend.\" Mentions \"project name\" not \"issue title.\"\n\n**Assessment**: The backend-design's original requirements are loosely worded compared to the detailed specs, but not a hard contradiction.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 15: Feature scope -- Module B vs. Module D boundary\n\n**0526 backend-design.md says**: Module B is \"Issue Global Management\" with functions B1-B5. Module D is \"Issue Skill Adaptation\" with D1-D3 (where D3 covers all subsequent skills: done/pr/test/review).\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says**: Module D has D1 through D7 as separate sub-modules (D1=claim, D2=fix, D3=done, D4=pr, D5=test, D6=review, D7=session-end).\n\n**0527 files say**: Module D has D0 through D7 as separate sub-requirements, matching the skill-integration-design's granularity but adding D0 (backend infra).\n\n**Files**: `claude-tap-plus-backend-design.md` vs. `claude-tap-plus-skill-integration-design.md` vs. `00-overview.md`\n\n**Assessment**: The backend-design uses a coarser granularity (D1, D2, D3) while both the 0526 skill-integration-design and 0527 files use finer granularity (D0-D7). The 0527 files added D0 as a new module for the shared infrastructure.\n\n---\n\n## Inconsistency 16: Claim write operation differs\n\n**0526 skill-integration-design.md says** (section 10, timing table): \"INSERT OR IGNORE issue_claims (idle) -> UPDATE status='claimed', session_id=xxx\"\n\n**0527 00-overview.md says** (timing table, line 166): \"INSERT OR IGNORE -> UPDATE status='claimed'\"\n\n**0526 issue-design.md says** (section 10.4): \"First check/claim: INSERT OR IGNORE (idle). Claim su