             # Client configuration (Claude Code)\n│   ├── proxy/\n│   │   ├── reverse.go              # Reverse proxy implementation\n│   │   ├── headers.go              # Header filtering and redaction\n│   │   ├── paths.go                # Allowed API path whitelist\n│   │   └── netutil.go              # Network utilities\n│   ├── session/\n│   │   ├── collect.go              # Session collection logic\n│   │   ├── meta.go                 # Session metadata structures\n│   │   ├── restore.go              # Session restoration logic\n│   │   ├── slug.go                 # Project slug generation\n│   │   └── status.go               # Session status reporting\n│   ├── sse/\n│   │   ├── reassembler.go          # SSE stream reconstruction\n│   │   └── types.go                # SSE type definitions\n│   ├── testutil/\n│   │   └── fixture.go              # Test utilities\n│   ├── trace/\n│   │   ├── anthropic.go            # Anthropic-specific trace handling\n│   │   └── writer.go               # JSONL trace writer\n│   └── usage/\n│       ├── anthropic.go            # Anthropic usage normalization\n│       └── normalize.go            # Multi-provider token normalization\n├── tests/                           # Test suites\n│   ├── e2e/\n│   │   └── proxy_trace_test.go     # End-to-end tests\n│   ├── proxy/\n│   │   ├── headers_test.go\n│   │   └── paths_test.go\n│   ├── session/\n│   │   └── parse_test.go\n│   ├── sse/\n│   │   └── reassembler_test.go\n│   ├── trace/\n│   │   └── writer_test.go\n│   └── usage/\n│       └── normalize_test.go\n├── .gitignore\n├── go.mod                           # Go module definition\n└── README.md                        # Project documentation\n```\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### 1. Go Module Name\n`github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus`\n\n### 2. Main CLI Structure (`cmd/claude-tap/main.go`)\nThe CLI has **4 subcommands**:\n\n- **Default (proxy mode)**: Runs a reverse proxy that intercepts Claude Code API traffic\n- **`session-push`**: Collects Claude sessions to local storage\n- **`session-pull`**: Restores sessions from local storage to `~/.claude/`\n- **`session-status`**: Shows session storage state\n\n### 3. Internal Package Structure\n\nThe `internal/` directory contains 6 main packages:\n\n- **`config/`**: Configuration management for Claude Code integration\n  - `claudeconfig.go`: Reads `~/.claude.json` config files\n  - `client.go`: Defines client-specific settings and target detection\n\n- **`proxy/`**: HTTP reverse proxy implementation\n  - `reverse.go`: Main proxy server with SSE handling\n  - `headers.go`: Header filtering and sensitive data redaction\n  - `paths.go`: API path whitelisting\n  - `netutil.go`: Cross-platform network utilities\n\n- **`session/`**: Session management functionality\n  - `collect.go`: Collect sessions from `.claude/` directory\n  - `restore.go`: Restore sessions back to `.claude/`\n  - `meta.go`: Session metadata structures\n  - `slug.go`: Project slug generation for unique identifiers\n  - `status.go`: Session status reporting\n\n- **`sse/`**: Server-Sent Events handling\n  - `reassembler.go`: Reassembles SSE chunks into complete API responses\n  - `types.go`: SSE type definitions\n\n- **`trace/`**: JSONL trace recording\n  - `writer.go`: Trace writer with token statistics\n  - `anthropic.go`: Anthropic-specific trace handling\n\n- **`usage/`**: Token usage normalization across providers\n  - `normalize.go`: Normalizes token fields for Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini\n  - `anthropic.go`: Anthropic-specific usage handling\n\n### 4. Additional Features\n- **Demo implementation** (`.00demo/`): Python version for comparison/development\n- **Comprehensive test suite** covering all major components\n- **Multi-provider support**: Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini API handling\n- **Sensitive data redaction**: API keys and tokens are masked in trace files\n- **Session synchronization**: Can backup/restore Claude sessions between machines\n\nThe project is a sophisticated reverse proxy that intercepts AI coding agent API traffic, records detailed traces, and provides session management capabilities for Claude Code."}]},{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore hooks structure","prompt":"Explore the existing hooks and skills structure in `D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk\\.claude\\`. I need to understand:\n\n1. The full hooks directory tree - all files under `.claude/hooks/`\n2. The full skills directory tree - all files under `.claude/skills/`\n3. The `settings.json` file\n4. Key hook scripts like `hooks/base.sh`, `hooks/platform.sh`\n5. Key skill scripts especially the 003 series (003-1 through 003-9)\n6. The `skills/backend.sh` if it exists\n7. The `skills/active.sh`, `skills/log.sh`, `skills/lock.sh` shared modules\n\nBe very thorough - I need a complete picture of the existing structure to redesign it.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"tool_use_id":"call_1230ee52e434430f94a311ae","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"\nBased on my thorough exploration of the `.claude` directory structure, here's a complete picture of the existing hooks and skills architecture:\n\n## Complete Structure Overview\n\n### 1. **Full Hooks Directory Tree**\n\nThe hooks directory contains **29 hook event types**, each with their own base script:\n\n```\n.claude/hooks/\n├── base.sh                           # Base hook script with logging and dispatch\n├── platform.sh                       # OS detection and Python resolution\n├── [01-29] directories (29 total):\n│   ├── 01-session-start/\n│   ├── 02-setup/\n│   ├── 03-user-prompt-submit/\n│   │   └── skill-inject.sh           # Skill injection trigger\n│   ├── 04-user-prompt-expansion/\n│   ├── 05-pre-tool-use/               # Tool boundary enforcement\n│   ├── 06-permission-request/\n│   │   └── win32-foreground.sh\n│   ├── 07-permission-denied/\n│   ├── 08-post-tool-use/\n│   ├── 09-post-tool-use-failure/\n│   ├── 10-post-tool-batch/\n│   ├── 11-notification/\n│   ├── 12-sub