├── 003-3-issue-discuss/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-4-issue-claim/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-5-issue-fix/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-6-issue-done/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-7-issue-pr/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-8-issue-test/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 003-9-issue-review/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 004-git-push/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init.sh\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   ├── 005-git-commit/\n│   │   ├── SKILL.md\n│   │   └── scripts/\n│   │       ├── init.sh\n│   │       ├── init_check.sh\n│   │       ├── 03UserPromptSubmit.sh\n│   │       └── 16Stop.sh\n│   └── 999-other-110-requirement-planning/\n│       ├── SKILL.md\n│       ├── references/\n│       │   ├── interview-guide.md\n│       │   └── templates.md\n│       └── (no init_check.sh)\n└── log/                              # Per-skill log directories\n```\n\n### 3. **settings.json Configuration**\n\nDefines **21 hook events** with command-based execution:\n\n- `SessionStart` to `SessionEnd` (events 01-29)\n- All hooks execute `base.sh` in their respective directories\n- Each hook has empty matcher (global trigger)\n\n### 4. **Key Hook Scripts**\n\n**base.sh** - The core hook engine:\n- Handles JSON input/output with fallback parsing\n- Provides unified logging to `hooks/logs/<date>.log`\n- Implements skill dispatch based on `.active` file\n- Maps hook events to skill lifecycle scripts\n\n**platform.sh** - Platform detection:\n- OS detection (Linux/macOS/Windows)\n- Python resolution with embedded fallback\n- Cross-platform compatibility layer\n\n### 5. **Key Skill Scripts (003 Series)**\n\n**003-1-issue-init**: GitHub label initialization\n- Reads `labels.conf` for tag definitions\n- One-time setup with marker file\n\n**003-2-issue**: Issue management\n- Local draft workflow (`doc/issues/drafts/`)\n- Template system (`doc/issues/templates/`)\n- Structured issue metadata\n\n**003-3-issue-discuss**: Issue discussion\n- Pulls issue content into session context\n- Comment-based interaction\n\n**003-4-issue-claim**: Atomic issue claiming\n- Prevents multi-agent conflicts\n- Handles rejected issues\n\n**003-5-issue-fix**: Branch creation\n- Auto-generates branch names\n- Type-based branch prefixes\n\n**003-6-issue-done**: Development completion\n- Status transition to ready-for-pr\n- Validation checks\n\n**003-7-issue-pr**: PR creation\n- Enforces Test Plan requirement\n- Automatic issue linking\n\n**003-8-issue-test**: Test execution\n- Checkbox tracking in PR body\n- Test validation workflow\n\n**003-9-issue-review**: PR approval\n- Test Plan completion verification\n- Merge/reject decisions\n\n### 6. **Shared Skill Modules**\n\n**active.sh** - Session management:\n- Maps session_id to skill_name\n- Atomic file operations with locking\n- CRUD operations for skill activation\n\n**log.sh** - Centralized logging:\n- Writes to both unified and module-specific logs\n- Timestamped with skill tag prefix\n\n**lock.sh** - File synchronization:\n- mkdir-based atomic locking\n- Timeout and zombie lock handling\n\n### 7. **Configuration Files**\n\n**dirs.conf** - Directory structure definitions:\n- Standardizes project directories\n- Used by `ensure_dirs.sh`\n\n**labels.conf** - GitHub label definitions:\n- Standardized issue tags\n- Color and description mappings\n\n**registry.conf** - Skill registry:\n- Lists all available skills\n- Used by skill injection system\n\n### 8. **Additional Components**\n\n**init.sh** - First-run initialization:\n- Directory creation\n- Python environment setup\n- UTF-8 configuration\n- Skill initialization\n\n**scripts/** - Utility modules:\n- `ensure_dirs.sh` - Directory management\n- `ensure_python.sh` - Python environment setup with auto-download\n\nThis architecture provides a comprehensive, event-driven system for skill management with robust logging, session isolation, and tool boundary enforcement. The 003 series implements a full GitHub issue lifecycle management workflow."}]}]}
